    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`MultiModalStaticCache.get(self, mm_hashes: List[int], combined_hash: Optional[int] = None)` accepts an optional precomputed `combined_hash` (matching the base `MultimodalCache.get` interface), but previously overwrote it unconditionally on the first line:\n```python\ncombined_hash = self.combine_hashes(mm_hashes)\n```\nAs a result:\n1. Any caller passing a precomputed `combined_hash` had its value ignored and `hash(tuple(mm_hashes))` recomputed.\n2. Both multimodal embedding cache callers (`_get_chunked_embedding_full` in `python/sglang/srt/managers/mm_schedule.py` and the disaggregated encoder cache lookup in `python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/encoder/server.py`) already compute `MultiModalStaticCache.combine_hashes(...)` immediately before calling `.get(...)`, causing `combine_hashes` to be computed twice on every multimodal request lookup.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- In `MultiModalStaticCache.get` (`python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/multimodal_cache.py`), only compute `self.combine_hashes(mm_hashes)` when `combined_hash is None`.\n- Pass the already-computed `combined_hash` in `_get_chunked_embedding_full` (`python/sglang/srt/managers/mm_schedule.py`) and in the disaggregated encoder server (`python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/encoder/server.py`).\n- Add a unit test (`test_multimodal_static_cache_reuses_precomputed_combined_hash`) in `test/registered/chunked_prefill/test_mm_chunked_embedding_unit.py`.\n\n### Acknowledgments\nFull credit to the SGLang multimodal caching and chunked prefill authors who designed `MultimodalCache` / `MultiModalStaticCache` and `mm_schedule.py`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format Code with Pre-Commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests as outlined in the [Running Unit Tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#running-unit-tests-adding-to-ci).\n- [x] Update documentation / docstrings / example tutorials as needed, according to [Writing Documentation](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#writing-documentation-and-example-tutorials).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #40292671102](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40292671102)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #40292671054](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40292671054)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #40292671225](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40292671225)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
